 39	Cloud model entries are keyed by normalized cloud base model name and verbose.
 40	They use stale-while-revalidate behavior: a warm read returns the cached
 41	response immediately and starts a throttled background refresh for that model.
 42	Cold cloud reads preserve existing proxy behavior. Local and cloud entries live
 43	in separate maps, so a local "qwen3.5" and an explicit "qwen3.5:cloud" cannot
 44	collide. The cloud suffix is request routing intent; api.ShowResponse does not
 45	carry a model-name field to reconstruct on the way out.
